// ============================================================================
// 01 - Suspicious IP triage (broad sweep, start here)
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Purpose : one row per client IP over a long window, with the signals that
//           separate a normal visitor from a scanner / brute-forcer:
//           write attempts (POST), error volume (401/403/404/5xx), and how
//           many distinct URLs it touched (URL fan-out = scanning behaviour).
// Use it  : first query of any investigation. Gives you the IPs and the
//           timestamps that you then drill into with queries 02/03/06.
// Table   : AppServiceHTTPLogs (Azure App Service, Log Analytics workspace)
//
// TUNABLES (see README section "01"):
//   ago(7d)                -> lookback window
//   make_set(..., 15)      -> number of example URLs kept per IP
//   posts > 5 / erreurs>30 -> noise floor; raise on busy sites, lower on quiet
//   sort by posts desc     -> swap to `erreurs` or `urls` to rank differently
// ============================================================================
AppServiceHTTPLogs
| where TimeGenerated > ago(7d)
| summarize
    requetes = count(),
    posts    = countif(CsMethod == "POST"),
    erreurs  = countif(ScStatus >= 400),
    urls     = dcount(CsUriStem),
    premier  = min(TimeGenerated),
    dernier  = max(TimeGenerated),
    exemples = make_set(CsUriStem, 15)
  by CIp
| where posts > 5 or erreurs > 30
| sort by posts desc
